INSERT INTO questions VALUES(76,replace('Top K News: \nThe interview process:\nI was shown the Bloomberg terminal for the news and how the most popular news appears. Also, I saw the selection for the time interval.\n-> So, the engineer mentioned that I should design a similar system that displays the most popular news and discuss the system components, storage and data model.\nQuestions asked -> How do I intend to get to aggregate the news counts as the services weren''t available and how to ensure this aggregation is not limited to one news window? -> Didn''t use the correct terms like event listeners-> was trying to say my services will sit between clients and the news feed and this didn''t go well. Perhaps best to say you have an event listener service that will keep track of the news visited by clients.\nEven if you say this, you will most likely get a question such as how do you mean the event handler operates. Don''t know if Message Queue is the right tools to handles this event but they seems fine when I made use of this.\nMore tricky questions kept coming and their body language wasn''t helping to know if you were always on the right track.\nAnother tricky question asked was on the use of Snapshot and how we claim these snapshots are stored in our key-value store. They have problem on how all news will keep growing row-wise and how will I handle such.-> I came up with elimination after 30 days but doesn''t seem like the best solution as they may have the old news referenced back and if it was already removed how did it work?\nFinally, I was asked a question regarding if my servers failed and how do I resolve the issues. -> This was the most tricky of it cos I felt we need to investigate them.\nOne takeaway was that I couldn''t make most of my point on choosing the tools to be used as questions kept coming and were tricky.\nThus my advice for future system design interviews is to have the flows you wanna take, be prepared for either high-level or low-level design and pramp with past Bloomberg interviewees. This will help to handle the tricky question.\nI feel some questions will test if you stand on your fundamentals so if you get tricky questions, it doesn''t mean you are not on the right track.','\n',char(10)),'3','technical',X'',5139431786,'2026-08-09 13:37:52');
INSERT INTO questions VALUES(77,'Design a system to manage custom indexes for our users. A custom index is an arithmetic expression that calculates a value based on the current prices of one or more securities (financial instruments). For example, “IBM equity + BP equity” is a custom index composed of the sum of the prices of IBM and BP stocks.','3','technical',X'',5139431786,'2026-08-09 13:38:18');
INSERT INTO questions VALUES(78,replace('Design a feature on the Bloomberg terminal. It was called a custom index.\nMore Details\nAn index/query a customer can subscribe to and get notified whenever the value of that query changes. For example, I can create a custom index called "myIndex" and the query will be "MSFT * APPL/GOOG + AMAZ". This means it should divide price of Apple''s stock by Google''s, then multiply by Microsoft''s and then add Amazon''s price. It will then return the value of that query, and you can choose to subscribe to get notified whenever the query changes. \nYou can use any arithmetic operation in your query and add as many companies as you like.','\n',char(10)),'3','technical',X'',5139431786,'2026-08-09 13:38:36');
INSERT INTO questions VALUES(79,replace('Design a system to manage Custom Indexes for our users. \nMore  details\nA custom index is an arithmetic expression that calculates a value based on the current prices of one or more securities (financial instruments). For example, “IBM Equity + BP Equity” is a custom index composed of the sum of the prices of IBM and BP stocks. \n\nThe system should offer the following functionality: \nAllow a user to create/modify/delete custom indexes. \nReturn the current value of a user’s custom index. \nThe design should include: \nThe major components of the system. \nThe APIs that the system present\nWhat data the system would store.','\n',char(10)),'3','technical',X'',5139431786,'2026-08-09 13:39:15');
